---The configuration for the session.
---@class gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionConfig
---@field entryAgent? string Optional. The entry agent to handle the session. If not specified, the session will be handled by the root agent of the app. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/apps/{app}/agents/{agent}`
---@field useToolFakes? boolean Optional. Whether to use tool fakes for the session. If this field is set, the agent will attempt use tool fakes instead of calling the real tools.
---@field includeLlmThoughtSummary? boolean Optional. Whether to include LLM thought summaries in the session outputs.
---@field inputAudioConfig? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.InputAudioConfig Optional. Configuration for processing the input audio.
---@field deployment? string Optional. The deployment of the app to use for the session. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/apps/{app}/deployments/{deployment}`
---@field enableTextStreaming? boolean Optional. Whether to stream text output from the model to the client incrementally as it is generated. Defaults to `false`. * When disabled, the model's text output is buffered, and each text output sent to the client is a complete sentence. Clients can render each text output on a new line. * When enabled, each text output may contain only part of a sentence. Clients should concatenate consecutive text outputs to render the complete response. NOTE: This is only supported for text (non-voice) sessions using StreamRunSession or BidiRunSession.
---@field includeProgressUpdate? boolean Optional. Whether to include intermediate processing update to the client. If enabled, the update will be sent back in SessionOutput.progress.
---@field outputAudioConfig? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.OutputAudioConfig Optional. Configuration for generating the output audio.
---@field historicalContexts? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.MessageList Optional. The historical context of the session, including user inputs, agent responses, and other messages. Typically, CES agent would manage session automatically so client doesn't need to explicitly populate this field. However, client can optionally override the historical contexts to force the session start from certain state.
---@field remoteDialogflowQueryParameters? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionConfigRemoteDialogflowQueryParameters Optional. [QueryParameters](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/reference/rpc/google.cloud.dialogflow.cx.v3#queryparameters) to send to the remote [Dialogflow](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/concept/console-conversational-agents) agent when the session control is transferred to the remote agent.
---@field excludeDiagnosticInfo? boolean Optional. Whether to exclude diagnostic info from the session output.
---@field timeZone? string Optional. The time zone of the user. If provided, the agent will use the time zone for date and time related variables. Otherwise, the agent will use the time zone specified in the App.time_zone_settings. The format is the IANA Time Zone Database time zone, e.g. "America/Los_Angeles".

---[QueryParameters](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/reference/rpc/google.cloud.dialogflow.cx.v3#queryparameters) to send to the remote [Dialogflow](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/concept/console-conversational-agents) agent when the session control is transferred to the remote agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionConfigRemoteDialogflowQueryParameters
---@field payload? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.DocumentMap Optional. The payload to be sent in [QueryParameters](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/reference/rpc/google.cloud.dialogflow.cx.v3#queryparameters).
---@field webhookHeaders? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.StringMap Optional. The HTTP headers to be sent as webhook_headers in [QueryParameters](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/reference/rpc/google.cloud.dialogflow.cx.v3#queryparameters).
---@field endUserMetadata? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.DocumentMap Optional. The end user metadata to be sent in [QueryParameters](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/cx/docs/reference/rpc/google.cloud.dialogflow.cx.v3#queryparameters).

---Input for the session.
---@class gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionInput
---@field toolResponses? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.ToolResponses Optional. Execution results for the tool calls from the client.
---@field audio? string Optional. Audio data from the end user.
---@field text? string Optional. Text data from the end user.
---@field dtmf? string Optional. DTMF digits from the end user.
---@field image? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.Image Optional. Image data from the end user.
---@field blob? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.Blob Optional. Blob data from the end user.
---@field recordingControl? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionInputRecordingControlEnum|string Optional. Whether the conversation may be recorded and logged from here on. Use this when the app, rather than the agent, decides what may be kept: for example when the end user has to consent to being recorded before anything about the call can be stored. The value stays in effect until the client sends a different one, so it only needs to be sent when the answer changes. Whatever is in effect when a turn completes decides that turn, both whether its audio reaches the recording bucket and whether its transcript reaches conversation history, BigQuery and Cloud Logging. It covers the agent's side of the turn as well as the end user's. Turns that complete before the client first sends this are recorded according to the app's logging settings, as though the field did not exist. If more than one input in the same request sets it, the last one wins.
---@field event? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.Event Optional. Event input.
---@field willContinue? boolean Optional. A flag to indicate if the current message is a fragment of a larger input in the bidi streaming session. When set to `true`, the agent defers processing until it receives a subsequent message where `will_continue` is `false`, or until the system detects an endpoint in the audio input. NOTE: This field does not apply to audio and DTMF inputs, as they are always processed automatically based on the endpointing signal.
---@field variables? gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.DocumentMap Optional. Contextual variables for the session, keyed by name. Only variables declared in the app will be used by the CES agent. Unrecognized variables will still be sent to the Dialogflow agent as additional session parameters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionInputList gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionInput[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.ces_v1beta.SessionInputRecordingControlEnum "RECORDING_CONTROL_UNSPECIFIED"|"RECORDING_ENABLED"|"RECORDING_DISABLED"

